Current Dev Position: YP 2.2 M1

Next Deadline: YP 2.2 cut off: June 13, 2016


SWAT team rotation: Anibal -> Tracy

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_Build_Failure_Swat_Team


Key Status/Updates:

*        Python3 testing is showing much higher success. There remain some =
small issues in eSDK, automated testing and toaster but the core now builds=
 reliably and successfully. The code is being cleaned up for submission nex=
t week.

*        The week was challenging due to the volume of patches combined wit=
h the python3 work, glibc changes breaking pseudo which made it into fedora=
 and a uninative upgrade we were testing, the glibc upgrade accidentally lo=
sing a key code change, an autobuilder not having python3 present and vario=
us other misc failures which took time to disentangle.

*        buildtools-tarball now contains python3 in preparation for the upg=
rade to python 3 in bitbake.

*        The minimum version requirement for python3 is looking to be pytho=
n 3.4 at this point.

*        WDD rose slightly

*        YP 1.8.2 is nearing QA completion, there were some issues which ar=
e still being investigated but are unlikely to block release

*        YP 2.0.2 is nearly ready to be built, just finalizing the patchset

*        meta-intel 5.0 released


Key YP 2.2 Dates:

*        YP 2.2 M1 cut off would be: 6/13/16

*        YP 2.2 M1 release would be: 6/24/16

*        YP 2.2 M2 cut off would be: 7/18/16

*        YP 2.2 M2 release would be: 7/29/16

*        YP 2.2 M3 cut off would be: 8/29/16

*        YP 2.2 M3 release would be: 9/9/16

*        YP 2.2 M4 cut off would be: 10/3/16

*        YP 2.2 M4 release would be: 10/28/16


